# DPI money-proof gate

## Train note (Upgrade 9)

On the **current watermark** (accounting `mfi_integration_v3.4.2.x`): there is **no** live `**/dpi/**/*.java` tree. Attach via `scripts/dpic/**`, `scripts/bin/dpi-*.sh`, and registry only.

Java under `trustt-platform-accounting/**/batchnew/dpi/**` lands on **3.7.1 / DPI feature** — when those paths exist in the checkout, treat edits there as in-scope for this gate (same proof chain).

## When this applies

Any change to `DpiAccrualCalculation*`, `DpiAccrualBooking*`, `DpiBilling*` (when present), or `scripts/dpic/**` verify SQL.

## Mandatory before declaring DPI fix done

1. **Static:** `bash scripts/bin/dpi-booking-posting-guard.sh` (blocks `dayBefore(end_date)` regression)
2. **SQL proof:** `bash scripts/bin/dpi-money-proof.sh` (post-EOD + billing UD)
3. **Ship-loop:** money tier auto-runs `dpic.posting_calendar_regression`, `dpic.cross_eod_replay_134497`, `dpic.billing_ud_next_emi` when calc/booking/billing touched (`resolve_ship_cases.py`)
4. **Full regression:** `bash scripts/bin/agent-ops.sh verify-dpi-proof` (includes cross-EOD replay)

## Do not

- Trust `batch.dpi_*` SUCCESS-only — row-level money is in SQL helpers under `scripts/dpic/sql/helpers/`
- Reuse interest-accrual verify SQL for DPI booking (`value_date` and posting-day model differ)
- Skip multi-day booking replay for go-live / 15th-EMI loans (SDCP-10497)

## DPI job order (EOD)

```
dpiAccrualCalculation → dpiAccrualBooking (replay each posting day) → dpiBilling
```

Billing reads `accrual_posting_date IS NOT NULL`; bills on **next EMI** ≤ business date (or maturity monthly path — not yet in default ship guard).
